solidcore
Copyright (c) 2026 The solidcore contributors

This product is a Rust port (a derivative work) of the SMLib and SM_API
components of USD BRep, https://github.com/NVIDIA-Omniverse/usd-brep
(v1.0.1, commit 3fd5b95), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
See ATTRIBUTION.md for exactly which upstream material is used.

The upstream work carries the following notice:

  USD BRep is Copyright (c) 2020-2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All
  rights reserved. NVIDIA-authored portions of this product are licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0, except where otherwise noted.

The upstream SMLib and SM_API source files carry the SPDX header:

  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Upstream third-party notices (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md at the pinned commit) cover
OpenUSD, oneTBB, hwloc, MaterialX, OpenSubdiv, CPython, HACL*, pybind11, the
UsdSolid proposals, usd-validation-nvidia, the repo bootstrap scripts and optional
Python GUI tooling. None of those components is part of SMLib or SM_API, and none
is used, ported or redistributed by solidcore, so no further third-party notices
apply.

Modifications: the C++ sources were translated to Rust and restructured (arena
topology, typed ids, error values instead of status codes, explicit kernel
state instead of a global context). Each ported Rust file names the upstream
file(s) it derives from in its header.

Colocad downstream modification (2026-11-15): the pinned STEP importer includes continuous projected extrema of bounded circles and ellipses when constructing planar parameter domains. Other curve/surface domains retain the previous behavior. Original geometry, tolerances and validation checks are unchanged. Source, patch and resulting-file SHA-256 values are recorded in third_party/solidcore.lock.json.

Colocad applies a downstream STEP cylinder-domain change in crates/step-brep/src/lib.rs to keep periodic trim reconstruction within the finite face window.

Colocad adds endpoint multiplicity details to the B-spline knot failure report in crates/solidcore/src/nurbs/b_spline_curve/p3.rs.

Colocad applies a downstream change in crates/step-brep/src/lib.rs to remove exactly zero-support endpoint poles after construction of a previously clamped STEP edge.
Colocad downstream modification: uv-metric-regularity.patch reuses the existing
conservative rational-quadratic bounds on the actual metric-mapped trim curve.
Identity metrics skip mapped clones; mapped regularity is isolated from the
main check. The pinned source revision, validation thresholds, topology checks
and generic solver fallback remain unchanged; see third_party/solidcore.lock.json.

Colocad modifies STEP export of spherical and conical trimmed faces to preserve face orientation after reflection. The source revision, patch and resulting hashes are recorded in third_party/solidcore.lock.json.
